Corresponding Source
--------------------
The public instance at https://the booking host runs this program. Under
AGPL section 13, everyone who interacts with it over a network is offered the
Corresponding Source of the running modified version: it is this repository, at
the tag named by the deployed image (deploy/<version>-rp.<n>).

The running instance carries a visible "Source" link on the booking page,
rendered by TymeslotWeb.Extensions.SourceOffer.

Secrets are not Corresponding Source and are not published: SECRET_KEY_BASE,
DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, SMTP and OAuth credentials live only in
an untracked .env. See .env.example for the shape.

Trademarks
----------
"Tymeslot" and the Tymeslot logo are trademarks of Diletta Luna OÜ (Tallinn,
Estonia) and are NOT licensed under the AGPL. Upstream's TRADEMARK.md requires
that a distributed modified version carry its own name and its own logo, and
permits stating that it is derived from Tymeslot. Accordingly:

  * this fork is named "Slate Scheduler", not Tymeslot;
  * the public booking pages carry the operator's own mark;
  * this notice states the derivation, which TRADEMARK.md expressly allows.

Slate Scheduler is neither affiliated with, nor endorsed or sponsored by,
Diletta Luna OÜ or the Tymeslot project.

Note on internal naming: the OTP application, Elixir module namespace, release
name, database role and session cookie remain `tymeslot`. These are internal
identifiers, not the product name or mark presented to users, and renaming them
would break restore compatibility for every existing database backup. The
product a user encounters is named and marked as Slate Scheduler throughout.

